   I am not sure about longevity; however, there were some studies showing
high proportion of short people among world-famous scientists, artists and
political leaders - as well as proportion of people with physical handicaps.

   The suggested explanation is that if they have physical features that
make any attempts to be a happy alpha-moron futile, they try to establish
themselves in non-physical areas. Maybe, lots of potential geniuses with
big/fit bodies were having too much fun having sex and beating their neighbors
to find time to realize their abilities...

   Also, if you have fewer visits to the bars, sex partners and fights,
and more education and - eventually - income, you will live longer.


   Things are changing though.
For TV debates, it's more important to look good than to have a great mind.
I heard that in 80% of American presidential elections the tallest guy won.

   In the (purely hypothetical case of a) society run by an atavistic-minded
crowd (say, a monkey tribe ;) ), bigger body size should bring better social
standing, popularity, power, money - and longevity.
                                                    
